        # SESSION-START TEAM GATE (binding): a session starts with NO team — a
        # team is NOT a precondition. mode=off is the default (upstream parity:
        # team_mode.enabled defaults to false) and means "no auto-provision, no
        # unconditional notice". The DECOUPLED mechanical gate is `autoRoute`
        # (default enabled): at the session's first pre-step it evaluates the
        # frozen complexity gate — trigger = (matchedSignals >= 2) OR
        # anyExplicitFlag, with signals A (a `team:` prefix or `!team`, the
        # marker is consumed), B (>=4 distinct deliverable verbs), C (>=3
        # enumerated lines / action verbs / clauses) and D (a `.mpd/plans/*.md`
        # artifact exists). On a hit it provisions the STAGED default team
        # (profile `mpd`, approval=required — nothing spawns until the user
        # approves the Web plan) and injects ONE startup notice saying the
        # session was routed by the gate. presets: [mpd] scopes the gate to
        # mpd-preset sessions (sessions without any preset, e.g. headless direct
        # runs, are covered too), and subagent/member sessions (they carry
        # parentSession) never qualify. The gate runs on the PRE-STEP, before any
        # sizing doctrine, so it can actually prevent a team.
        # mode=auto keeps the legacy unconditional provisioning as an explicit
        # opt-in; mode=instruct keeps the legacy instruction notice.

